  "id": "BIT-grafana-2026-110289",
  "summary": "Git Sync connections send credentials to unvalidated server URLs",
  "details": "A user with the Organization Admin role could point the server or token URL of a Git Sync connection at a loopback or internal address, and Grafana would then send the connection's OAuth client secret and tokens, or requests signed with the GitHub App private key, to that address (server-side request forgery).",
